      ":question/problem": "Find the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(-15^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that*\n\n$$\n-15^\\circ=30^\\circ-45^\\circ.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x-y)=\\cos x\\cos y+\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(-15^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(30^\\circ-45^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(45^\\circ\\right)+\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(45^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
